{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>It is too much for you, sons of Levi.</b> [The sense is:] that which He has given to you. And he proceeds to explain afterward, ״המעט מכם כי הבדיל אלהי ישראל אתכם״ — 'Is it too little for you that the Elohim of Israel has separated you' — from the rest of the tribes." "<b>And know</b> that you will not find in all this perashah that Moses mentions in all his words anything but the distinctive Name (השם המיוחד); but here, since he mentioned 'sons of Levi,' he needed to mention 'the Elohim of Israel,' to allude to their quality."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:54.770238448Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}